# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Resend: newsletter capture + contact form
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local dev, and set the same values
# as environment variables in the hosting provider for production.
# While RESEND_API_KEY is empty both routes run in test mode: they log
# to the server console and return success, so the UI flow works end to
# end without an account.
#
# Setup order:
#   1. Verify the sending domain in Resend. Use the SUBDOMAIN
#      `send.maitstudio.com`, not the apex: the apex MX has to stay
#      pointed at the inbox provider (Cloudflare Email Routing), or
#      incoming mail to hello@maitstudio.com breaks.
#   2. Create the API key  ->  https://resend.com/api-keys
#   3. Deploy again. Env vars are baked in at build time.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Account key. One key covers both routes below. Without it, nothing is
# ever sent and the forms silently succeed.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# ── Newsletter (POST /api/subscribe) ─────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Resend retired Audiences in favour of Segments, and contacts
# now exist at account level, so a subscriber needs no list ID at all.
# Set this only to file new subscribers into one specific segment.
# There is no longer a RESEND_AUDIENCE_ID; if you are looking for one in
# the dashboard, that is why you cannot find it.
RESEND_SEGMENT_ID=

# ── Contact form (POST /api/contact) ─────────────────────────────────
# CONTACT_FROM must sit on the domain verified in step 1. Resend rejects
# a From it cannot authenticate. Nobody replies to it: the route sets
# Reply-To to the enquirer's own address.
CONTACT_FROM="MAIT Studio <hello@send.maitstudio.com>"

# Where enquiries land. This one is the real inbox that gets read, and
# Cloudflare Email Routing forwards it on.
CONTACT_TO="hello@maitstudio.com"
